3. She has a British background but modified her natural accent for better understandability. (Verbatim: "i'm actually kind of um what'd you call it um i i'm not actually posh mate i'm trying to hide my farmer accent")
4. Her natural regional British accent is difficult for even native English speakers to understand. (Verbatim: "if i spoke in a completely natural armarelli accent english people can't understand like native english native english speakers can't understand the accent")
5. She is half Asian, with her mother being Asian and having taught her American English. (Verbatim: "i'm half asian so she has she was taught american english and so she taught me a lot of american words")
6. She struggles with maintaining her original regional accent due to deliberate suppression. (Verbatim: "i actually cannot properly do it anymore um because it's been bored out of me")
7. She is preparing for a rockin' karaoke relay event on Sunday, indicating an interest or involvement in singing. (Verbatim: "i'm doing like my um i'm doing like a rockin karaoke relay on sunday")
8. She has previously practiced singing songs, including ones involving screaming, which temporarily affected her voice. (Verbatim: "i was practicing singing them and one of them was like more of a screaming kind of one so i was like practicing that and and it turns out that your voice... borked a little yesterday")
9. She feels emotionally overwhelmed by her community’s support and values bringing happiness to her viewers. (Verbatim: "thank you so much for everyone wishing me happy one year... i'm here to try and bring you smiles")
10. She does not feel like a seasoned VTuber despite her one-year milestone and believes she has much to learn. (Verbatim: "I still feel like there's a lot for me to learn a lot for me to get ahead and yeah I I mean that's why I still work so hard") [end of text]



1. She lives alone in an apartment building and describes herself as an elusive, reclusive neighbor. (Verbatim: "i'm the mystery being i'm a i'm a the elusive neighbor that rarely emerges from from her from her place")

2. She has a strong dislike of encountering neighbors in the hallway, calling it a "human jump scare." (Verbatim: "it's the human jump scare oh my gosh i went out the other day and i was jump scared by an entire family")

3. She finds it difficult to sleep due to noisy neighbors, especially one upstairs who frequently tries and fails to flirt with people late at night. (Verbatim: "it's always at some stupid o'clock and it wakes me up at like 2am and i'm like i just want to be like shush shush")

4. She lived in university halls known for constant noise, pranks, and disturbances like false fire alarms and broken windows. (Verbatim: "uni halls are an experience in themselves... the fire alarm was just set off for funsies like it was painful")

5. During university, she was frequently woken up by loud neighbors, including one who sang "Titanium" repeatedly. (Verbatim: "guy on the left who got broken up with by her girlfriend and spent the year singing sad songs... mostly that song um titanium")

6. She experienced surreal and chaotic events at university, such as a roommate throwing another girl’s entire bedroom out the window. (Verbatim: "this girl went into this other girl's room locked herself in... and then eating everything she owned in the room out of the window")

7. She recalls a university prank where a student’s belongings were removed and covered in kitchen foil in the hallway. (Verbatim: "take all his stuff out of his room and put it in the corridor and cover it in kitchen foil")

8. She was disturbed by bats flying in the university corridor, but expressed sympathy for the animals. (Verbatim: "woken up by a bunch of screaming because there was some bats or something like flying around the corridor and i'm like just let the bats live")

9. She associates Akihabara’s Mr. Donuts with a “VTuber pilgrimage,” indicating a sentimental or ritual significance. (Verbatim: "i need to do my vtuber pilgrimage you're right yeah yeah i wanted to do it like before but when i was there last time it was like peak time")

10. She humorously identifies with the concept of being a “goose” or in “denial,” suggesting it's part of her online persona or community in-joke. (Verbatim: "i'm not in denial i'm not a goose and i can't deny the banana and bias") [end of text]



